   "text": "I read the molecule region by region and wrote the SMILES from that reading. The stereocentre assignments come from the drawing conventions, not from a database match.\n\n**Peptide (left side):** H2N\u2011Gly\u2011Gly\u2011Gly\u2011Lys\u2011Val\u2011Cit. The lysine side chain is a 4\u2011aminobutyl group and the citrulline side chain ends in a urea (NHC(=O)NH2). I took all three amino acids as L, written as `N[C@@H](R)C(=O)`.\n\n**Linker:** the citrulline NH is attached to a para\u2011aminobenzyl group, which is joined through a carbamate to N\u2011methyl\u2011N,N'\u2011ethylene\u2011N'\u2011methyl diamine. That diamine's second nitrogen forms a carbamate to the phenol oxygen of the alkylating unit.\n\n**Alkylating unit:** this is a seco\u2011CBI (benzo[e]indoline) core carrying:\n- a 1\u2011(chloromethyl) group;\n- a methyl on the naphthalene ring, adjacent to the ring\u2011fusion carbon bonded to C1;\n- the carbamate\u2011bearing oxygen on the naphthalene ring, para to the ring\u2011fusion carbon that bears the indoline nitrogen.\n\nThe indoline nitrogen is acylated.\n\n**Stereocentre at C1:** the CH2Cl bond is hashed. The CIP priorities are CH2Cl > C2 (the CH2 bonded to N) > C9b (the aromatic ring\u2011fusion carbon) > H. With H toward the viewer, CH2Cl \u2192 C2 \u2192 C9b runs clockwise, so the centre is S. In the SMILES written as `C[C@@H](CCl)c2`, `@@` gives S.\n\n**DNA\u2011binding tail:** the acyl group is an imidazo[1,2\u2011a]pyridine\u20112\u2011carbonyl. Its 6\u2011position carries an NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013C6H4\u2013OH amide (4\u2011hydroxybenzamide).\n\nSMILES: NCC(=O)NCC(=O)NCC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(N)=O)C(=O)Nc1ccc(COC(=O)N(C)CCN(C)C(=O)Oc2cc3N(C(=O)c4cn5cc(NC(=O)c6ccc(O)cc6)ccc5n4)C[C@@H](CCl)c3c3c(C)cccc23)cc1"
